\"If a 'Report Incident' activity occurs, then an 'Assess Impact' activity must eventually occur after the 'Report Incident' event at some point in the same process instance, within a time window between 0 and 24 hours. There is no requirement on how soon or what events may occur in between. Multiple 'Report Incident' events can be pending at the same time, and a single 'Assess Impact' can fulfill the obligation for all preceding 'Report Incident' events. If 'Report Incident' does not occur, the constraint imposes no obligation on the occurrence of 'Assess Impact'.\",\"template\":\"Response\",\"activation\":{\"name\":\"Report Incident\",\"description\":\"The 'Report Incident' activity represents the initial step of logging a new incident into the system.\"},\"target\":{\"name\":\"Assess Impact\",\"description\":\"The 'Assess Impact' activity involves evaluating the severity and consequences of the reported incident.\"},\"activation_condition\":null,\"correlation_condition\":null,\"time_condition\":\"0,24,h\",\"cardinality\":null},{\"type\":\"binary\",\"description\":\"An 'Assess Impact' activity must be followed by a 'Prioritize Incident' activity at some point later in the same process instance. Conversely, a 'Prioritize Incident' event can occur only if an 'Assess Impact' event has occurred before it within the same process instance. This bidirectional and ordered dependency ensures that 'Assess Impact' imposes obligations for future 'Prioritize Incident', and 'Prioritize Incident' cannot occur without prior 'Assess Impact'. Multiple 'Assess Impact' and 'Prioritize Incident' are allowed, with each 'Assess Impact' eventually leading to a 'Prioritize Incident' and each 'Prioritize Incident' being justified by a preceding 'Assess Impact'.\",\"template\":\"Succession\",\"activation\":{\"name\":\"Assess Impact\",\"description\":\"The 'Assess Impact' activity involves evaluating the severity and consequences of the reported incident.\"},\"target\":{\"name\":\"Prioritize Incident\",\"description\":\"The 'Prioritize Incident' activity assigns a priority level to the incident based on its assessed impact.\"},\"activation_condition\":null,\"correlation_condition\":null,\"time_condition\":null,\"cardinality\":null},{\"type\":\"binary\",\"description\":\"The 'Prioritize Incident' activity is permitted to occur only if an 'Assign Incident' activity has occurred before it within the same process instance, when the correlation condition 'T.Priority in (High, Critical)' is satisfied, meaning the 'Priority' attribute of the target event is either 'High' or 'Critical'. 'Prioritize Incident' events that occur without any prior 'Assign Incident' are violations of the constraint. Multiple 'Assign Incident' events can occur, and any number of events can happen between an 'Assign Incident' and a subsequent 'Prioritize Incident'.\",\"template\":\"Precedence\",\"activation\":{\"name\":\"Prioritize Incident\",\"description\":\"The 'Prioritize Incident' activity assigns a priority level to the incident based on its assessed impact.\"},\"target\":{\"name\":\"Assign Incident\",\"description\":\"The 'Assign Incident' activity designates a responsible team to handle the incident.\"},\"activation_condition\":null,\"correlation_condition\":\"T.Priority in (High, Critical)\",\"time_condition\":null,\"cardinality\":null},{\"type\":\"binary\",\"description\":\"The 'Investigate Incident' activity is permitted to occur only if a 'Resolve Incident' activity has occurred before it within the same process instance. 'Investigate Incident' events that occur without any prior 'Resolve Incident' are violations of the constraint. Multiple 'Resolve Incident' events can occur, and any number of events can happen between a 'Resolve Incident' and a subsequent 'Investigate Incident'.\",\"template\":\"Precedence\",\"activation\":{\"name\":\"Investigate Incident\",\"description\":\"The 'Investigate Incident' activity entails examining the incident to identify its root cause and potential solutions.\"},\"target\":{\"name\":\"Resolve Incident\",\"description\":\"The 'Resolve Incident' activity involves implementing a fix or solution to address the incident.\"},\"activation_condition\":null,\"correlation_condition\":null,\"time_condition\":null,\"cardinality\":null},{\"type\":\"binary\",\"description\":\"If a 'Resolve Incident' activity occurs, then a 'Verify Resolution' activity must eventually occur after the 'Resolve Incident' event at some point in the same process instance, within a time window between 0 and 48 hours. There is no requirement on how soon or what events may occur in between. Multiple 'Resolve Incident' events can be pending at the same time, and a single 'Verify Resolution' can fulfill the obligation for all preceding 'Resolve Incident' events. If 'Resolve Incident' does not occur, the constraint imposes no obligation on the occurrence of 'Verify Resolution'.\",\"template\":\"Response\",\"activation\":{\"name\":\"Resolve Incident\",\"description\":\"The 'Resolve Incident' activity involves implementing a fix or solution to address the incident.\"},\"target\":{\"name\":\"Verify Resolution\",\"description\":\"The 'Verify Resolution' activity confirms whether the applied resolution has successfully resolved the incident.\"},\"activation_condition\":null,\"correlation_condition\":null,\"time_condition\":\"0,48,h\",\"cardinality\":null},{\"type\":\"binary\",\"description\":\"If a 'Verify Resolution' activity occurs and the activation condition 'A.Verification Result is Failed' is satisfied, meaning the 'Verification Result' attribute of the activation event is 'Failed', then an 'Escalate Incident' activity must eventually occur after the 'Verify Resolution' event at some point in the same process instance. There is no requirement on how soon or what events may occur in between. Multiple 'Verify Resolution' events can be pending at the same time, and a single 'Escalate Incident' can fulfill the obligation for all preceding 'Verify Resolution' events. If 'Verify Resolution' does not occur or the activation condition is not satisfied, the constraint imposes no obligation on the occurrence of 'Escalate Incident'.\",\"template\":\"Response\",\"activation\":{\"name\":\"Verify Resolution\",\"description\":\"The 'Verify Resolution' activity confirms whether the applied resolution has successfully resolved the incident.\"},\"target\":{\"name\":\"Escalate Incident\",\"description\":\"The 'Escalate Incident' activity raises the incident to a higher level of support or management when resolution efforts are insufficient.\"},\"activation_condition\":\"A.Verification Result is Failed\",\"correlation_condition\":null,\"time_condition\":null,\"cardinality\":null},{\"type\":\"binary\",\"description\":\"A 'Close Incident' activity must be followed by a 'Document Incident' activity at some point later in the same process instance. Conversely, a 'Document Incident' event can occur only if a 'Close Incident' event has occurred before it within the same process instance. This bidirectional and ordered dependency ensures that 'Close Incident' imposes obligations for future 'Document Incident', and 'Document Incident' cannot occur without prior 'Close Incident'. Multiple 'Close Incident' and 'Document Incident' are allowed, with each 'Close Incident' eventually leading to a 'Document Incident' and each 'Document Incident' being justified by a preceding 'Close Incident'.\",\"template\":\"Succession\",\"activation\":{\"name\":\"Close Incident\",\"description\":\"The 'Close Incident' activity formally marks the incident as closed after verification is complete.\"},\"target\":{\"name\":\"Document Incident\",\"description\":\"The 'Document Incident' activity records all relevant details and actions taken regarding the incident for future reference.\"},\"activation_condition\":null,\"correlation_condition\":null,\"time_condition\":null,\"cardinality\":null},{\"type\":\"unary\",\"description\":\"The 'Escalate Inciden